        "verdict": {
          "approved": true,
          "summary": "Reviewed the complete head 929fcf5 of reconciliation PR #442 (main->dev, base 975775f, baseIsAncestor=true, first-parent ancestry reaches base with the expected two-parent merge, changed-path count=4, no gitlinks). The diff hardens release check verification in .github/scripts/df-release.mjs: check-run/commit-status/check-suite/workflow-run inventories are now completely paginated with bounded limits and double-scan fingerprint consistency; evaluateRequiredChecks collects all same-name candidates and fails closed on app-id ambiguity; and policy checks reporting under the shared GitHub Actions app id (15368) are bound to their exact trusted workflow file, ref, event, same-repo (non-fork) provenance, and pull/branch evidence via bindTrustedPolicyCheckRuns, with pull_request runs additionally requiring the head workflow file blob to equal the base definition. The df-audit.yml change replaces hashFiles gating with a deterministic report_exists step output while preserving node exit-code propagation. Trust-boundary review confirms untrusted head content is treated as data, release logic stays in df-release.mjs, no provider/model/runtime mechanics are embedded, no managed-file or protected-ref write path is introduced, and tests under tests/ cover the new runtime branches (ambiguity, wrong app, missing/malformed/truncated/oversized/changing inventories, and each provenance-rejection case). No correctness, security, regression, or coverage defect blocks this exact head.",
